# Which models/articles/judges to run — tracked in git (unlike
# /etc/eval-harness.env, which holds secrets and is never committed).
# Edit this file, commit, `git pull` on the droplet, then
# `sudo systemctl restart eval-harness` to pick it up. Already-completed
# (model, article) pairs are cached and won't be redone.
#
# Same flags as `python3 scripts/eval_harness.py run` locally — see
# eval/README.md. Split on whitespace (at use, in run.sh), so no argument
# here can contain a space (none of these flags need one).
#
# MUST stay double-quoted: this file is bash-`source`d (not parsed by
# systemd's more forgiving EnvironmentFile format), so an unquoted value
# with spaces is read as "set RUN_ARGS=--models, then run the next word as
# a command" — bash tries to execute the first model slug as a program and
# fails with "No such file or directory".
# qwen3-235b-a22b dropped: 10/10 gen errors in do-batch-1 (OpenRouter 404 —
# "No endpoints available matching your guardrail restrictions and data
# policy"), meaning its providers don't meet the account's ZDR/no-training
# policy. Re-add only after confirming it shows up in the account's
# ZDR-filtered model list.
#
# Current roster (descriptions also shown on the dashboard/`status` output —
# see scripts/eval/model_catalog.py, update both when the roster changes):
#   qwen/qwen3-30b-a3b        lightweight MoE (~3B active / 30B total), open weight
#   google/gemma-3-27b-it     dense 27B, open weight
#   google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it lightweight MoE (~4B active / 26B total), open weight
#   qwen/qwen3.8-27b          dense 27B, open weight
#   google/gemini-3.7-flash   frontier closed model, proprietary
#   openai/gpt-5.6-luna       fast/affordable tier of GPT-5.6, proprietary
#   z-ai/glm-5.3-flash        fast/affordable tier of GLM 5.3, closed model, proprietary
#
# z-ai/glm-5.3-flash added to register it as an available model ahead of an
# auto-optimize experiment scoped to just this model (see
# glm-5.3-flash-test-1/-2 in eval/runs/index.html for its standalone-run
# results once they finish). Adding it here does NOT take effect on the
# always-on eval-harness service until this file is git-pulled on the
# droplet and the service is restarted (`sudo systemctl restart
# eval-harness`) — do that deliberately, since it extends whatever
# do-batch-2 is currently mid-run on, not as a side effect of an unrelated
# change. If glm-5.3-flash-test-1/-2 turn out to hit the
# reasoning-token-burn failure mode qwen3.8-27b has (see
# model_catalog.REASONING_DISABLED), fix that before restarting the service
# with this roster.
#
# --judges includes "gemini" alongside opus/gpt specifically because
# openai/gpt-5.6-luna is now a model UNDER TEST above — an OpenAI judge
# grading an OpenAI model's own extraction is a self-review conflict of
# interest, so gemini (an independent model family, via OpenRouter) is kept
# in the judge panel for every model, not just gpt-5.6-luna's results. See
# scripts/eval/judge.py's judge_with_gemini().
#
# qwen/qwen3.8-27 (no trailing "b") was a typo'd slug — OpenRouter returned
# "not a valid model ID" (HTTP 400) for every article in do-batch-2. The
# correct slug is qwen/qwen3.8-27b. Since the dirname derived from a model
# slug changes with it (see safe_model_dirname() in eval_harness.py), the
# corrected model started fresh with no cached results — no --overwrite
# needed for the fix itself.
#
# IMPORTANT: delete the broken slug's leftover directory rather than leaving
# it — compute_rows() in eval_harness.py aggregates every model subfolder it
# finds on disk, with no awareness of what's still in RUN_ARGS above, so a
# stale all-errors directory shows up forever as a phantom extra "model"
# (0.0s latency, no judge score) in every chart and the exec summary:
#   rm -rf eval/runs/do-batch-2/qwen__qwen3.8-27
#   rm -rf eval/runs/do-batch-1/qwen__qwen3-235b-a22b   # same issue, from the guardrail-404 drop above
# then regenerate: python3 scripts/eval_harness.py report --run-id <run-id>
RUN_ARGS="--models qwen/qwen3-30b-a3b google/gemma-3-27b-it google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it qwen/qwen3.8-27b google/gemini-3.7-flash openai/gpt-5.6-luna z-ai/glm-5.3-flash --judges opus gpt gemini --run-id do-batch-2"
